# Smart home / consumer IoT — ENORMOUS IDLE CONNECTION COUNT, bursty.
#
# Tens of millions of devices, each mostly silent; mobile apps subscribe to
# their own device's topics. Very high connection:message ratio, and sudden
# thundering herds when an ISP segment reconnects. What matters is memory per
# connection and establishment rate, not throughput — lane C's shape.
LANES=C
LANE_C_CONNS=50000
LANE_C_RAMP=2500
LANE_C_HOLD=120
# Sweep the workload's own axis by overriding per run:
#   LANE_C_CONNS=50000|100000|200000|500000 (raise LANE_C_RAMP with it)
# Tuning levers: MQTTD_MAX_CONNECTIONS, MQTTD_MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_IP,
#   MQTTD_MEMORY_MAX_BYTES, MQTTD_TLS_SESSION_CACHE (reconnect storms).
